load @term/seed/structure/function/unary
  find unary-function

# A fixed point: a point a map leaves unmoved, where the input equals the output. Fixed points are equilibria, the
# solutions a process settles to, and the fixed-point theorems (Brouwer, Banach) guarantee they exist under the right
# conditions. The self type at the bottom of the type theory names the fixed point of a family. The form carries the map
# whose fixed point is sought.
form fixed-point
  link map, like unary-function
